    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Rare Coastal Home with Exceptional Flexibility & Income Potential\r\n\r\nWelcome to an exceptional coastal residence in the heart of Cromane, County Kerry, where breathtaking scenery, remarkable flexibility and an enviable seaside lifestyle combine to create a truly unique property.\r\n\r\nJust a leisurely two-minute stroll from the shoreline and moments from the beautiful Rossbeigh and Glenbeigh beaches, this beautifully presented residence enjoys an outstanding coastal setting with sea views from parts of the property. Offering exceptional flexibility together with outstanding lifestyle and income potential, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a home that can adapt effortlessly to a wide range of purchasers.\r\n\r\nThoughtfully designed to incorporate two self-contained residences within the one property, this exceptional home has successfully operated as a spacious family residence while simultaneously generating additional income through guest accommodation. Whether you are seeking an impressive family home, a multi-generational residence, a coastal retreat, or a property with established income potential, the possibilities here are truly exceptional.\r\n\r\nThe principal residence offers bright and generously proportioned accommodation comprising two spacious bedrooms, welcoming reception rooms, a well-appointed kitchen, separate dining room and two bathrooms.\r\n\r\nThe second self-contained residence provides a further three bedrooms, three bathrooms, a comfortable sitting and dining room together with a practical galley kitchen, making it ideal for extended family, independent living, long-term guests or continued holiday accommodation.\r\n\r\nAdding yet another layer of versatility is the detached chalet nestled within the garden. Beautifully presented, it offers one spacious bedroom, a bathroom and an open-plan living, dining and kitchen area, creating the perfect guest suite, home office, private retreat or an additional source of income.\r\n\r\nThe entire property has been lovingly maintained and is presented in excellent decorative order throughout, allowing its new owners to simply unpack and begin enjoying everything this exceptional coastal home has to offer.\r\n\r\nThe location is every bit as impressive as the property itself. Positioned within easy walking distance of the renowned Jack’s Coastguard Restaurant, celebrated as one of Kerry’s most beloved seafood destinations, and the ever-popular The Boathouse Café, residents can enjoy superb dining, exceptional coffee and relaxed seaside living right on their doorstep. The beaches at Rossbeigh and Glenbeigh are just moments away, offering endless opportunities for swimming, paddle-boarding, sailing, kayaking, fishing or simply enjoying spectacular coastal walks along the Wild Atlantic Way. Golf enthusiasts will also appreciate being less than a five-minute drive from the prestigious Dooks Golf Club, one of Ireland’s oldest and most celebrated championship links courses.\r\n\r\nDespite its wonderfully peaceful setting, the property is only a short drive from the vibrant town of Killorglin, where an excellent range of supermarkets, schools, churches, cafés, restaurants, pharmacies, sporting facilities and everyday amenities await. Kerry Airport is also within easy reach, while the bustling tourist town of Killarney can be reached in approximately 40 minutes, placing world-class golf courses, Killarney National Park, Muckross House, luxury hotels and countless recreational opportunities comfortably within reach.\r\n\r\nProperties offering this degree of flexibility, coastal charm and proven income potential rarely become available. Combining beautifully presented accommodation, multiple independent living spaces, an enviable seaside location and exceptional lifestyle appeal, this is a truly unique opportunity to secure one of Cromane’s most versatile and desirable homes."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
